# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lakeshore_shore_walk
# en: The Long Way Round
title [250a85] = 绕远路
# en: {You came out to walk alone. {date} finds you on the shore path and falls into step without asking.|The shore path is where you go to think. Today {date} has the same idea.|You know every stone of the shore path by now. Today {date} walks it with you.} {season == "winter": The lake is frozen at the edges and your breath walks ahead of you.|{season == "summer": The water is warm and full of sky.|{Mist lies on the water like a sheet someone forgot to fold.|The towers stand upside down in the lake, lit window by lit window.}}}
text [8e507f] = {你本想独自走走。{date}在湖岸小径上遇见你，没问一声就和你并肩走了起来。|湖岸小径是你想事情的地方。今天{date}也是这么想的。|湖岸小径上的每块石头你都认得了。今天{date}陪你走。} {season == "winter": 湖边结了冰，你的呼吸走在你前面。|{season == "summer": 湖水温暖，盛满了天空。|{雾铺在水面上，像一张忘了叠的床单。|七塔倒映在湖里，一扇亮窗接着一扇亮窗。}}}
# en: Two figures walking a lakeside path at dusk, the towers reflected upside down in the still water beside them.
scene [33361d] = 黄昏时两个人影走在湖边小径上，身旁静水里倒映着颠倒的高塔。
# en: Walk the long way round
opt.left.label [793774] = 绕远路走一圈
# en: {final_year: Halfway round, {date} says "next year" and stops, because there won't be one here. You walk the rest closer together.|{season == "winter": {You walk until your toes go numb. {date} lends you {their} scarf and pretends not to be cold.|The ice sings under your boots. {date} takes your arm on the slippery stretch and forgets to let go.}|{You walk until the far lamps go out. Neither of you mentions the time.|{date} points out a lit tower window and tells you who lives behind it. Half of it is invented. You don't mind which half.|You stand at the water's edge in silence, and the silence is the good kind.}}}
opt.left.say.1 [6487a6] = {final_year: 走到一半，{date}说了句“明年”，又停住了，因为在这里不会再有明年。剩下的路，你们靠得更近。|{season == "winter": {你们一直走到你的脚趾冻僵。{date}把围巾借给你，假装自己不冷。|冰在你们靴子下歌唱。走到滑的那段，{date}挽住你的胳膊，忘了松开。}|{你们一直走到对岸的灯火一盏盏熄灭。谁也没提时间。|{date}指着一扇亮着的塔窗，告诉你里面住的是谁。一半是编的。你不在乎是哪一半。|你们在水边默默站着，那是很好的那种沉默。}}}
# en: Talk about anything but us
opt.right.label [9c9439] = 聊什么都行，别聊我们
# en: {You talk about exams, the cook and the weather. It's easy. It's also not what either of you came for.|You argue cheerfully about whether the lake has a bottom. It's a good walk. It's only a walk.}
opt.right.say.1 [df4829] = {你们聊考试、聊厨娘、聊天气。很轻松。也不是你们俩来这里想说的。|你们兴致勃勃地争论这湖到底有没有底。散步很愉快。也只是散步。}

@event lakeshore_cold_swim
# en: The Cold Swim
title [242756] = 冷水游泳
# en: {season == "winter": Students in towels are daring each other into the lake through a hole in the ice.|{season == "summer": Half the academy is in the lake; the other half pretends not to want to be.|A few hardy students are swimming out to the flat rock, shrieking.}} {The water looks inviting. It always does.|You know how cold the Mirror Lake really is. You're tempted anyway.|You and the lake have an understanding. It doesn't help.}
text [be4c03] = {season == "winter": 几个裹着毛巾的学生正互相怂恿，要从冰窟窿里跳进湖去。|{season == "summer": 半个学院都泡在湖里，另一半在假装自己不想下水。|几个不怕冷的学生正往平顶岩游去，一路尖叫。}} {湖水看上去很诱人。它一向如此。|你知道镜湖实际上有多冷。可你还是心动了。|你和这片湖之间有某种默契。这并没有用。}
# en: Students in towels on a lakeshore, one wading in up to the knees and shrieking, the towers reflected behind them.
scene [7cec80] = 湖岸上裹着毛巾的学生们，一个人蹚水到膝盖，正在尖叫，身后倒映着高塔。
# en: Brave the water
opt.left.label [5f5f4d] = 下水试试
# en: {season == "winter": You go under, come up roaring, and are hauled out a hero.|{You slap the flat rock, whoop, and swim back to applause from people with dry hair.|You reach the rock first. The cold reaches you second, but you were already winning.}}
opt.left.say.1 [7e2519] = {season == "winter": 你沉下去，吼着冒出头，被当成英雄拖上了岸。|{你一掌拍上平顶岩，欢呼一声，在一群头发干爽的人的掌声中游了回来。|你第一个碰到岩石。寒冷第二个碰到你，可你已经赢了。}}
# en: {You come back blue to the lips and sneezing. Sister Amaranth sighs before you've even sat down.|Halfway out, the lake reminds you who is in charge. You turn back with what dignity you have left.}
opt.left.say.2 [225fb4] = {你回来时嘴唇发青、喷嚏连天。你还没坐下，阿玛兰斯修女就先叹了口气。|游到一半，湖水提醒你谁才是主人。你带着仅剩的体面掉头回来。}
# en: Hold the towels and heckle
opt.right.label [a0e0ba] = 帮忙拿毛巾，顺便起哄
# en: {You announce every dive like a herald. You're dry, popular and a tiny bit jealous.|You keep the towels warm and the commentary warmer. Someone throws a wet sock at you, which is fair.}
opt.right.say.1 [f0dfeb] = {你像传令官一样播报每一次跳水。你很干爽、很受欢迎，也有一点点嫉妒。|你把毛巾捂得暖暖的，解说更热烈。有人朝你扔了一只湿袜子，这很公平。}

@event duel_hall_dummies
# en: The Practice Dummies
title [01b66d] = 练习假人
# en: {The near end of the hall belongs to the practice dummies, who watch you come in. The one with the painted moustache looks especially unforgiving.|The dummy with the moustache is still here, with a new scorch mark and, you'd swear, a new grudge.|The moustached dummy greets you with its usual silence. Someone has given it an eyepatch.} {The floorboards are still warm from the last session.|A singed glove lies abandoned on the rack.|Rain drums on the high windows.}
text [4bdf3a] = {大厅近端归练习假人所有，它们看着你进门。那个画了小胡子的看起来格外不肯原谅人。|画小胡子的假人还在，多了一道焦痕，你敢发誓，还多了一份怨气。|小胡子假人照例沉默地迎接你。有人给它戴了个眼罩。} {地板还留着上一场练习的余温。|架子上丢着一只烧焦的手套。|雨点敲打着高窗。}
# en: An empty duelling hall with scorched floorboards and a row of battered straw practice dummies, one with a painted moustache.
scene [ddc84f] = 空荡的决斗厅，地板满是焦痕，一排破旧的草扎练习假人，其中一个画着小胡子。
# en: Drill your hexes on it
opt.left.label [74919a] = 拿它练咒
# en: {Hex after hex until your wrists ache. The dummy loses a sleeve and none of its contempt.|You land a clean one at last. A wisp of straw floats down, slowly, like applause.}
opt.left.say.1 [c227f1] = {一道咒语接一道咒语，直到手腕发酸。假人掉了一只袖子，轻蔑却一分没少。|你终于打出一记干净利落的。一缕稻草慢慢飘落，像是掌声。}
# en: Restuff the battered ones
opt.right.label [218ba9] = 给破假人重新填草
# en: {You haul a bale of straw over from the stables and restuff three dummies. They look almost grateful, which is unsettling.|You restuff the moustached one with special care. It still looks like it's planning something.}
opt.right.say.1 [862cc1] = {你从马厩扛来一捆稻草，给三个假人重新填好。它们看上去几乎心怀感激，这让人不安。|你格外用心地给小胡子假人填了草。它看上去还是在盘算着什么。}

@event duel_hall_gallery
# en: From the Gallery
title [f73290] = 看台之上
# en: {From the gallery above the duelling floor you can watch whoever is practising. Today it's {here}.|You've learned to read duels from up here. Today {here} is drilling.|The gallery rail has a groove where you lean. Below, {here} is drilling.} {Sparks drift up to the gallery rail.|Somebody's familiar is asleep on the scoreboard.|The ceiling has acquired a new scorch mark.}
text [d11fa8] = {从决斗场上方的看台，你能看到谁在练习。今天是{here}。|你已经学会从这上面看懂决斗了。今天{here}在练。|看台栏杆上有一道你常倚的凹痕。下面，{here}在练。} {火星飘上看台的栏杆。|不知谁的使魔睡在记分板上。|天花板又添了一道新焦痕。}
# en: A narrow wooden gallery above a duelling floor, one student watching another drill spells at a target below.
scene [5292ba] = 决斗场上方狭窄的木制看台，一个学生看着下面另一个对着靶子练咒。
# en: Offer to spar
opt.left.label [ed03b2] = 提出陪练
# en: {You take a round off {here}. {They} stare{s} at you for a long second, then ask{s} for another.|You win with a feint you stole from watching {here}. {They} notice{s}, and look{s} annoyed and pleased at once.}
opt.left.say.1 [e95c78] = {你从{here}手里拿下一局。{They}盯着你看了好一会儿，然后要求再来一局。|你用看{here}练习时偷学的虚招赢了。{They}看出来了，又恼又高兴。}
# en: {{here} puts you on the floorboards, politely. From down there the ceiling's scorch marks make a sort of map.|{here} disarms you so neatly that the dummies seem to wince. Your wand skids under the gallery stairs.}
opt.left.say.2 [eea003] = {{here}很有礼貌地把你放倒在地板上。从下面看，天花板上的焦痕像是一张地图。|{here}缴械缴得干净利落，连假人都像是缩了一下。你的魔杖滑进了看台楼梯底下。}
# en: Watch and take notes
opt.right.label [d829ad] = 看着记笔记
# en: {You fill a page with what {here} does with {their} feet. You'll never get to try it, and you know it.|You sketch {here}'s guard from above. On paper it has a gap. On the floor it doesn't.}
opt.right.say.1 [2a06f6] = {你把{here}的步法记了满满一页。你永远不会有机会试，你也知道。|你从上方画下{here}的防守架势。纸上有个破绽。场上没有。}

@event duel_hall_humming_circle
# en: The Humming Circle
title [1a4455] = 嗡鸣的法阵
# en: {The evening bouts are over. At the near end of the hall the warding circle is still humming.|The warding circle is humming. Whoever's drilling at the far end isn't looking your way.|The circle hums. You know its tune by now.} {final_year: Soon someone else will be sneaking in here after hours.|{A practice wand lies on the rack, still warm.|The steward's broom leans by the door, watching.|Tonight the ceiling stain looks like a dragon.}}
text [52ec0c] = {晚上的比试结束了。大厅近端的护界法阵还在嗡嗡作响。|护界法阵在嗡鸣。远处练习的人没往你这边看。|法阵在嗡鸣。你已经熟悉它的调子了。} {final_year: 很快就会有别人在闭馆后溜进这里了。|{架子上放着一根练习魔杖，还是温的。|管理员的扫帚靠在门边，像在盯着你。|今晚天花板上的污渍看起来像一条龙。}}
# en: A dark duelling hall lit only by a ring of faintly glowing runes on the floor.
scene [939412] = 漆黑的决斗厅，只有地上一圈微微发光的符文照明。
# en: Step in and try a hard one
opt.left.label [9c5c46] = 走进去试个难的
# en: {The spell comes out clean and the circle drinks it. Somewhere a dummy loses its head and nobody ever finds out how.|You try the thing you saw a fourth-year do. It works. You tell no one, and walk back grinning.}
opt.left.say.1 [a178da] = {咒语干净利落地打出，法阵把它吞了下去。某处一个假人掉了脑袋，没人知道是怎么回事。|你试了一招见四年级生用过的。成功了。你谁也没告诉，一路笑着走回去。}
# en: {The circle hands your spell straight back to you. Your eyebrows will regrow.|The circle flares, the dummies rattle, and you leave very quickly before the steward arrives.}
opt.left.say.2 [338679] = {法阵把你的咒语原样还给了你。你的眉毛会长回来的。|法阵一闪，假人们哗啦作响，你赶在管理员来之前飞快地溜了。}
# en: Sweep up for the steward
opt.right.label [b29618] = 替管理员扫地
# en: {You sweep up a winter's worth of ash. The steward pays you a few crowns and a grunt that might be thanks.|You sweep. The circle hums at you the whole time, like a cat that wants to be let out.}
opt.right.say.1 [79afe7] = {你扫掉了一整个冬天的灰烬。管理员给了你几枚克朗，外加一声可能是道谢的哼哼。|你扫着地。法阵一直冲你嗡嗡叫，像一只想出门的猫。}

@event greenhouses_warm_glass
# en: The Warm Glass
title [4d5441] = 温暖的玻璃
# en: {season == "winter": Outside it's snowing. Inside, the glass runs with warm water and everything smells of earth.|{season == "summer": The greenhouses are sweltering, and everyone has retreated to the far end where the vents are.|The greenhouses steam gently. Someone is singing to the mandrakes at the far end.}} {You find a dry corner by the ferns, out of everyone's way.|Someone has left a cushion in your corner by the ferns.|The ferns lean toward you when you come in, as they do for you now.}
text [4ff1a0] = {season == "winter": 外面在下雪。里面，玻璃上淌着温热的水珠，到处是泥土的气味。|{season == "summer": 温室里闷热难当，大家都躲到了有通风口的那一头。|温室里轻轻蒸腾着水汽。远处有人在给曼德拉草唱歌。}} {你在蕨类旁找到一个干爽的角落，不碍任何人的事。|有人在你蕨类旁的那个角落里留了个垫子。|你一进门，蕨类就朝你探过来，如今它们一向如此。}
# en: A student reading on an upturned pot among tall ferns inside a steamy glass greenhouse, snow on the panes outside.
scene [9eaa5e] = 雾气蒸腾的玻璃温室里，一个学生坐在倒扣的花盆上，在高高的蕨类间读书，窗外落着雪。
# en: Do your reading in the warm
opt.left.label [2d902a] = 在暖和处读书
# en: {You get through a whole chapter. The pages curl in the damp and you come out smelling of moss.|You read until the steam makes the ink run. What's left of the chapter sticks.}
opt.left.say.1 [899b7d] = {你读完了整整一章。书页在潮气里卷了边，你出来时一身青苔味。|你一直读到水汽把墨迹洇开。剩下的那部分章节倒是记住了。}
# en: Nap on the potting bench
opt.right.label [8ac69b] = 在盆栽台上打个盹
# en: {You wake with a seed tray for a pillow and a first-year staring at you. By supper it's a story.|You wake to a mandrake humming a lullaby. You choose not to tell anyone. Someone tells everyone.}
opt.right.say.1 [6c3e0f] = {你醒来时枕着育苗盘，一个一年级生正盯着你。到晚饭时，这已经成了一段故事。|你在曼德拉草哼的摇篮曲里醒来。你决定谁也不告诉。有人告诉了所有人。}

@event greenhouses_repotting
# en: Repotting Day
title [5b9bc1] = 换盆日
# en: {here} is up to the elbows in compost, repotting {season == "spring": seedlings that have outgrown everything|{season == "autumn": bulbs for the winter|something with more teeth than leaves}}. {"Hands?" {they} ask{s}.|{They} hand{s} you a trowel before you've said hello.|There's a trowel on the hook that has come to be yours. {here} nods at it.}
text [36e480] = {here}正把胳膊埋在堆肥里，给{season == "spring": 长得什么都装不下的幼苗|{season == "autumn": 准备过冬的球根|一株牙齿比叶子还多的东西}}换盆。{“搭把手？”{they}问。|你还没打招呼，{They}就递给你一把小铲子。|钩子上有一把小铲子，渐渐成了你的。{here}朝它点点头。}
# en: A student elbow-deep in compost at a greenhouse bench, handing a trowel to someone arriving.
scene [c4461e] = 温室工作台边，一个学生胳膊深埋在堆肥里，把小铲子递给刚到的人。
# en: Get your hands dirty
opt.left.label [f6a380] = 动手干活
# en: {You repot a whole row. Something nips your thumb in thanks.|You're filthy, nipped and oddly happy. {here} says you have good hands for roots.}
opt.left.say.1 [d05cf1] = {你给一整排换了盆。有什么东西咬了一下你的拇指，算是道谢。|你满身泥污，被咬了几口，却莫名开心。{here}说你天生一双侍弄根的手。}
# en: Ask questions, stay clean
opt.right.label [d36613] = 光提问，不沾手
# en: {You learn a great deal about soil. {here} learns that you're afraid of it.|You take notes. {here} gives you a look over the trowel that says notes are not hands.}
opt.right.say.1 [d51b65] = {你学到了很多关于泥土的知识。{here}则学到了你怕泥土。|你记着笔记。{here}隔着小铲子看了你一眼，意思是笔记不能代替手。}

@event greenhouses_cuttings
# en: The Cuttings Bench
title [c5d8ff] = 插条台
# en: {A row of silver-leaf cuttings is drying on the bench|A tray of night-orchid cuttings sits by the door|A bundle of moonpetal cuttings is wrapped in damp cloth}, and Pell & Daughters pays well for that sort of thing. {Nobody is watching. The snapdragons are.|The snapdragons have seen you here before. They remember.|The snapdragons snap at you on principle now.}
text [31a502] = {台子上晾着一排银叶插条|门边放着一盘夜兰插条|一捆月瓣花插条裹在湿布里}，佩尔父女药铺收这种东西出价不低。{没人在看。金鱼草在看。|金鱼草以前见过你。它们记得。|金鱼草现在出于原则见你就咬。}
# en: A greenhouse bench of labelled cuttings drying in rows, a row of snapdragons with actual teeth watching from their pots.
scene [4762ee] = 温室工作台上一排排晾着的插条，带标签，一排长着真牙齿的金鱼草在盆里盯着。
# en: Pocket a cutting
opt.left.label [44bf20] = 偷偷揣一根插条
# en: {Pell's counts the leaves twice and pays without a question. You don't look at the snapdragons on your next visit.|It sells for more than you expected, which somehow makes it worse.}
opt.left.say.1 [0527dd] = {佩尔家把叶子数了两遍，二话不说付了钱。下次来时你没敢看金鱼草。|它卖的价钱比你想的还高，不知怎么反而更糟了。}
# en: {A snapdragon shrieks. Three Verdant students turn around at once. You put it back with a cough that convinces no one.|Your pocket rustles at the wrong moment. You spend the rest of the visit apologising to a fern.}
opt.left.say.2 [05bb85] = {一株金鱼草尖叫起来。三个青翠社的学生同时回头。你干咳一声把它放回去，谁也没被说服。|你的口袋在最不该的时候沙沙作响。这一趟剩下的时间，你都在向一株蕨类道歉。}
# en: Feed the snapdragons
opt.right.label [22dfda] = 喂金鱼草
# en: {They take the food, then a little of your finger. You learn which end to hold the tongs by.|Fed, the snapdragons purr like kettles. One of them still bites you, out of habit.}
opt.right.say.1 [3de298] = {它们吃了食物，又顺带吃了一点你的手指。你学会了夹子该拿哪一头。|吃饱的金鱼草像水壶一样咕噜咕噜。还是有一株咬了你，出于习惯。}

@event flight_field_cheating_wind
# en: The Cheating Wind
title [c14839] = 耍赖的风
# en: {season == "winter": The flight field is white, the hoops wearing caps of snow.|{season == "spring": The field is soft with new grass and the wind is playful.|{The field is empty but for the wind, practising on its own.|A lone first-year is flying very careful circles.}}} {The school brooms in the shed are, at best, opinionated.|Your usual broom is in the shed, the one that pulls left.|The broom that pulls left now pulls right, out of spite.}
text [5c307d] = {season == "winter": 飞行场一片雪白，圈门都戴上了雪帽。|{season == "spring": 场地铺满柔软的新草，风很调皮。|{场上空无一人，只有风在自己练习。|一个一年级生在小心翼翼地绕圈飞。}}} {棚里的学校扫帚，往好里说，也是很有主见。|你常用的那把扫帚在棚里，就是总往左偏的那把。|那把往左偏的扫帚现在往右偏了，纯属赌气。}
# en: A long green field with tall hoops at either end, one student wobbling on a school broom against a gusting wind.
scene [7ab1d7] = 两端立着高高圈门的长条绿地上，一个学生骑着学校扫帚在阵风里摇摇晃晃。
# en: Practise your landings
opt.left.label [516481] = 练习降落
# en: {A dozen landings. A few of them on purpose. The grass keeps a careful record of the rest.|The wind waits until you're nearly down, then shoves. You land in a hoop instead. Technically, a goal.}
opt.left.say.1 [436f58] = {降落了十几次，其中几次是故意的。草地仔细记下了其余的。|风等你快落地时才推了一把。你落进了圈门里。严格来说，算进球。}
# en: Hire a decent broom
opt.right.label [cee8bc] = 租一把像样的扫帚
# en: {The good broom goes where you look, not where it feels like. For an hour, flying is easy and the field is yours.|You fly the length of the field and back with the wind on your side for once. It costs a week's sweets.}
opt.right.say.1 [6b1a51] = {好扫帚会去你看的地方，而不是它想去的地方。有那么一个钟头，飞行很轻松，整个场地都是你的。|你顺着风飞了个来回，这可是头一回。代价是一周的零食钱。}

@event flight_field_pickup_race
# en: The Pick-Up Race
title [22c25a] = 临时赛
# en: {A pick-up race is forming at the far hoops. Three brooms, two rules, no referee.|The pick-up racers are back. The rules have grown to four.|The pick-up race is a fixture now. Someone has painted a finish line, crookedly.} {A second-year from Emberhall is taking bets.|A Brasswick student has bolted a lantern to their broom-tail.|A Rootward student is flying barefoot, for grip.}
text [9c1159] = {远处的圈门那边正在凑一场临时赛。三把扫帚，两条规则，没有裁判。|临时赛的人又来了。规则涨到了四条。|临时赛已经成了固定节目。有人歪歪扭扭地画了一条终点线。} {一个烬厅的二年级生在坐庄。|一个铜芯的学生在扫帚尾巴上拴了盏灯笼。|一个根庐的学生光着脚飞，说是为了抓得牢。}
# en: Three students on brooms jostling at a crooked painted start line, a fourth holding up a scarf as a starting flag.
scene [66b550] = 三个骑扫帚的学生在一条歪斜的起跑线前推搡，第四个人举着围巾当发令旗。
# en: Borrow a broom and race
opt.left.label [18a85c] = 借把扫帚去比赛
# en: {You win by a broom's length and a lot of shouting. The second-year taking bets has to pay out and never forgives you.|You take the last hoop sideways and cross first. Someone adds a new rule, about you.}
opt.left.say.1 [535af9] = {你以一扫帚之差、外加一片叫喊声获胜。那个坐庄的二年级生只好赔钱，从此再没原谅你。|你侧着身子穿过最后一个圈门，第一个冲线。有人加了一条新规则，是关于你的。}
# en: {You finish last, and partly in a hedge.|The wind takes your side, then changes its mind. You walk the broom back to the start.}
opt.left.say.2 [c83475] = {你最后一名到达，有一部分是在树篱里到达的。|风先站在你这边，然后又改了主意。你推着扫帚走回起点。}
# en: Bet a few crowns on the outsider
opt.right.label [abc686] = 押几枚克朗给冷门
# en: {The outsider wins on a gust nobody else saw coming. You are suddenly very good at betting.|The outsider comes in first by a nose. You toast the nose.}
opt.right.say.1 [809b8a] = {冷门借着一阵谁也没料到的风赢了。你突然成了押注高手。|冷门以一个鼻尖的优势夺冠。你为那个鼻尖干杯。}
# en: {The outsider stops halfway to admire the view. Your crowns go with them.|Your flyer is disqualified for a rule invented on the spot. You don't argue. It's a good rule.}
opt.right.say.2 [3ed52c] = {冷门飞到一半停下来欣赏风景。你的克朗也跟着去了。|你押的人因为一条当场发明的规则被取消资格。你没争辩。那是条好规则。}

@event flight_field_long_grass
# en: The Long Grass
title [f6b1e4] = 长草丛
# en: {The long grass at the edge of the flight field catches everything that falls off a broom.|Someone has planted a little flag in the long grass, to mark where things land.|You've come to think of the long grass as the academy's real lost-and-found.} Today it's {a velvet glove|a letter with no envelope|a single boot, laced|someone's notes for an exam}. {season == "autumn": The leaves are trying to bury it.|{season == "winter": It's half under frost.|A grasshopper is sitting on it.}}
text [ea6dd5] = {飞行场边的长草丛接住了所有从扫帚上掉下来的东西。|有人在长草丛里插了面小旗，标出东西落下的地方。|你已经把长草丛当成学院真正的失物招领处了。}今天是{一只天鹅绒手套|一封没有信封的信|一只系好鞋带的靴子|某人的考试笔记}。{season == "autumn": 落叶正想把它埋起来。|{season == "winter": 它有一半埋在霜里。|一只蚱蜢正坐在上面。}}
# en: The long grass at the edge of a flight field, scattered with things dropped from brooms, a student crouching to look.
scene [b64b13] = 飞行场边的长草丛里散落着从扫帚上掉下的东西，一个学生蹲下来查看。
# en: Keep what you find
opt.left.label [86edf0] = 捡到就归我
# en: {The owner lands right beside you while you're still holding it. There's a short, very long silence.|A second-year marches over the grass shouting "Thief!" at the sky in general and you in particular.}
opt.left.say.1 [03001b] = {你还拿在手里，失主就在你旁边落了地。接下来是一阵短暂而又漫长的沉默。|一个二年级生大步穿过草地，冲着天空泛泛地大喊“小偷！”，具体来说是冲着你。}
# en: {Finders, keepers. The grass doesn't argue, and neither does your conscience, much.|Nobody comes looking. You tell yourself that settles it.}
opt.left.say.2 [d40511] = {谁捡到归谁。草丛没意见，你的良心也没多大意见。|没人来找。你告诉自己这就算了结了。}
# en: Carry it to the porter's lodge
opt.right.label [e8195a] = 送到门房去
# en: {It's a long walk round the field. The porter writes it in a book and gives you a look of mild surprise.|The porter thanks you with a peppermint from a jar that has clearly been open since the founders.}
opt.right.say.1 [1753ce] = {绕场一圈可不近。门房把它记进本子，略带惊讶地看了你一眼。|门房从一个显然自创始者时代就开着的罐子里掏出一颗薄荷糖谢你。}

@event stables_owl_loft
# en: The Owl Loft
title [2be609] = 猫头鹰阁楼
# en: {Up the ladder, above the hippogriffs, is a hay loft full of owls and quiet.|The owls open one eye each, decide you're furniture, and go back to sleep.|The owls have stopped opening their eyes for you. You've been accepted.} {season == "winter": The warmth of the animals rises through the boards.|{Rain ticks on the roof.|A stray letter has fallen into the hay.|The griffon chick is complaining somewhere below.}}
text [449aa4] = {爬上梯子，在鹰头马身有翼兽的上方，是一间满是猫头鹰和安静的干草阁楼。|猫头鹰们各睁开一只眼，认定你是件家具，又睡了。|猫头鹰们已经懒得为你睁眼了。你被接纳了。} {season == "winter": 动物们的暖意透过木板升上来。|{雨点滴答敲着屋顶。|一封走失的信掉进了干草里。|楼下的狮鹫幼崽在什么地方抱怨。}}
# en: A hay loft in old stables, rows of sleepy owls on the rafters above a student reading by a lantern.
scene [d922b6] = 老马厩的干草阁楼里，椽子上一排排睡眼惺忪的猫头鹰，下面一个学生就着灯笼读书。
# en: Read up among the owls
opt.left.label [928968] = 在猫头鹰中间读书
# en: {You read until the light goes. The hay gets in everywhere, and the chapter gets in too.|An owl reads over your shoulder for a whole page, then hoots, pointedly, at a footnote.}
opt.left.say.1 [a56c2c] = {你一直读到天黑。干草钻得到处都是，书里的内容也钻进了脑子。|一只猫头鹰趴在你肩上读了整整一页，然后意味深长地冲一条脚注叫了一声。}
# en: Help sort the owl post
opt.right.label [37a567] = 帮忙分拣猫头鹰邮件
# en: {You sort a dropped bundle of post by hand. One owl seems to know which letters you're going to misfile.|You deliver three soggy letters to their owners on the way back. One of them hugs you, which you weren't ready for.}
opt.right.say.1 [848562] = {你亲手整理了一捆掉落的信件。有只猫头鹰似乎早就知道你会放错哪几封。|回去路上你把三封湿漉漉的信交给了收信人。其中一个人抱住了你，你完全没准备好。}

@event stables_brask_rounds
# en: Brask's Rounds
title [11370d] = 布拉斯克巡厩
# en: {Professor Brask is on her rounds, telling each hippogriff she's a very good girl. She tells you to mind the bucket.|Brask is on her rounds. She nods at you, which is more than most get.|Brask greets you by name now, somewhere after the owls.} {season == "spring": There are new hippogriff foals, all legs and beak.|{A hippogriff is sulking about its feathers.|The feed is late and everyone is cross.|The stable cat is asleep in the oats.}}
text [794b64] = {布拉斯克教授正在巡厩，挨个告诉每只鹰头马身有翼兽它是个好姑娘。她让你当心水桶。|布拉斯克在巡厩。她冲你点了点头，这比大多数人得到的都多。|布拉斯克现在会叫你的名字了，排在猫头鹰后面。} {season == "spring": 新生的小兽崽全是腿和喙。|{一只鹰头马身有翼兽在为自己的羽毛闹脾气。|饲料送晚了，大家都很暴躁。|马厩的猫睡在燕麦堆里。}}
# en: A burly professor stroking a hippogriff's beak in a stable aisle, ignoring a student holding two feed buckets.
scene [5fb5c2] = 魁梧的教授在马厩过道里抚摸一只鹰头马身有翼兽的喙，无视旁边拎着两桶饲料的学生。
# en: Ask Brask a question
opt.left.label [3880c8] = 向布拉斯克请教
# en: {She answers it at length, to the hippogriff. You take notes anyway.|"Good question," she says, to the owl. You decide that counts.}
opt.left.say.1 [b170a9] = {她详详细细地回答了，对着那只鹰头马身有翼兽。你还是记了笔记。|“好问题，”她对猫头鹰说。你决定这也算数。}
# en: Carry the feed buckets
opt.right.label [2dfcee] = 帮忙提饲料桶
# en: {Every stall, two buckets each. Brask says nothing, which is his way of saying thank you.|A hippogriff bows to you over its bucket. Brask looks almost jealous.}
opt.right.say.1 [550efb] = {每个隔间两桶。布拉斯克一言不发，这就是他道谢的方式。|一只鹰头马身有翼兽隔着饲料桶向你鞠了一躬。布拉斯克看起来几乎有点嫉妒。}

@event stables_griffon_sulk
# en: The Sulking Griffon
title [16bcc6] = 闹别扭的狮鹫
# en: {The griffon chick is sulking in the corner stall, feathers puffed, refusing breakfast.|The griffon chick is sulking again. It's bigger this time, and so is the sulk.|The griffon is hardly a chick any more, and still sulks like one. It watches you come in.} {year == 1: The sign on the stall says not to hand-feed it, underlined twice.|{The sign on the stall now has a drawing of a bitten hand.|The sign on the stall has been underlined until the paper tore.|Someone has added "I mean it" to the sign, in Brask's hand.}}
text [05bcf4] = {狮鹫幼崽缩在角落的隔间里生闷气，羽毛炸着，不肯吃早饭。|狮鹫幼崽又在生闷气。它长大了些，闷气也大了些。|那只狮鹫已经算不上幼崽了，生起闷气来还和从前一样。它看着你进门。} {year == 1: 隔间上的牌子写着不许手喂，下面画了两道线。|{隔间的牌子上现在画了一只被咬的手。|隔间牌子上的线被画到纸都破了。|有人在牌子上添了句“我是认真的”，是布拉斯克的笔迹。}}
# en: A griffon chick with puffed-up feathers glaring from the corner of a stall, a student holding out a morsel at arm's length.
scene [63efe8] = 一只羽毛炸起的狮鹫幼崽在隔间角落里怒视，一个学生伸直胳膊递出一小块食物。
# en: Offer it breakfast by hand
opt.left.label [1ec395] = 亲手喂它早饭
# en: {It considers you for a long time, then takes the morsel with great delicacy. You feel chosen.|It eats from your hand and then, briefly, leans on you. You don't move for ten minutes.}
opt.left.say.1 [c23623] = {它打量了你很久，然后极其斯文地叼走了那块食物。你觉得自己被选中了。|它从你手里吃了东西，然后短暂地靠在你身上。你十分钟没敢动。}
# en: {It takes the morsel, a corner of your sleeve and a nip of your thumb. The sign was right.|It turns its back on you so pointedly that a passing owl looks embarrassed, and its tail catches you hard across the shins on the way round.}
opt.left.say.2 [803b05] = {它叼走了食物、你袖子的一角，还啄了一下你的拇指。牌子说得没错。|它转过身去背对你，刻意得连路过的猫头鹰都替你尴尬；转身时它的尾巴狠狠扫过你的小腿。}
# en: Leave it to its sulk
opt.right.label [bcf991] = 随它生闷气
# en: {You read the notice about griffon moods instead. It is mostly a list of things that will not help.|You leave it alone. It looks, as you go, a little disappointed you gave up.}
opt.right.say.1 [d20b20] = {你转而读起了关于狮鹫脾气的告示。上面大部分是一张“这些都没用”的清单。|你没去打扰它。你走的时候，它看上去有点失望你就这么放弃了。}

@event boathouse_jetty_end
# en: The End of the Jetty
title [d7bf11] = 栈桥尽头
# en: {{date} is at the end of the jetty, boots over the water. {They} move{s} over without a word.|The end of the jetty has become your place for saying things. Today {date} is already there.|You know which plank creaks. {date} doesn't, and finds it.} {season == "winter": The lake has frozen round the posts and creaks like an old house.|{The rowing boats knock gently together.|A heron fishes in the shallows, pretending not to listen.|The village lamps blink on across the water.}}
text [c3f932] = {{date}坐在栈桥尽头，靴子悬在水面上。{They}一句话没说，挪出了位置。|栈桥尽头成了你说心里话的地方。今天{date}已经在那儿了。|你知道哪块木板会响。{date}不知道，一脚就踩上了。} {season == "winter": 湖水在桩子周围结了冰，像老房子一样吱嘎作响。|{划艇轻轻地互相碰撞。|一只苍鹭在浅水里捕鱼，假装没在听。|对岸小镇的灯一盏盏亮起来。}}
# en: Two people sitting side by side at the end of a wooden jetty, boots over dark water, a lantern between them.
scene [738e69] = 两个人并肩坐在木栈桥尽头，靴子悬在黑色的水面上，中间放着一盏灯笼。
# en: Hire a boat and row out
opt.left.label [d01173] = 租条船划出去
# en: {season == "winter": You can't row on ice, so you sit in a beached boat and pretend. {date} calls it a fine voyage.|{You row badly, {date} laughs, and then neither of you is rowing at all.|Out in the middle the shore goes quiet. {date} says your name like the end of a sentence.}}
opt.left.say.1 [5efcda] = {season == "winter": 冰上没法划船，你们就坐在搁浅的船里假装。{date}说这是一趟不错的航行。|{你划得很糟，{date}笑你，然后谁也不划了。|划到湖心，岸上的声音都静了。{date}念你的名字，像在说一句话的结尾。}}
# en: Stay on the jetty and talk
opt.right.label [dedd57] = 留在栈桥上聊天
# en: {final_year: You talk about where you'll both be next year. Neither of you says "together", and both of you hear it.|{You talk until the lantern gutters. The jetty is cold and you don't notice until you stand.|You say one of the things you couldn't say indoors. {date} listens all the way to the end.}}
opt.right.say.1 [d91699] = {final_year: 你们聊起明年各自会在哪里。谁也没说“一起”，可两个人都听见了。|{你们一直聊到灯笼的火苗摇摇欲灭。栈桥很冷，站起来时你才发觉。|你说出了一件在屋里说不出口的事。{date}一直听到了最后。}}

@event boathouse_green_boat
# en: The Leaky Green Boat
title [c4a35d] = 漏水的绿船
# en: {The boathouse smells of tar and old rope. Its rowing boats are mostly leaks held together by paint, the green one worst of all.|Someone has patched the green boat since your last visit, badly, with what looks like a cake tin.|The boathouse knows you. The green boat still leaks.} {Initials are carved into every beam, some so old they've gone soft.|Rain patters on the roof.|A spider has strung a web across the oars, and seems proud of it.}
text [c1e87e] = {船屋里是焦油和旧绳子的气味。这里的划艇大多是用油漆粘在一起的漏洞，绿色那条最糟。|自你上次来过，有人给绿船打了补丁，打得很烂，用的像是个蛋糕模子。|船屋认得你。绿船还在漏水。} {每根房梁上都刻着姓名缩写，有些老得已经模糊了。|雨点轻敲着屋顶。|一只蜘蛛在船桨间结了网，看样子很得意。}
# en: Inside an old wooden boathouse, an upturned green rowing boat on trestles, initials carved into every beam above.
scene [4e9c10] = 老旧木船屋里，一条绿色划艇倒扣在支架上，上方每根房梁都刻满了姓名缩写。
# en: Patch the green boat
opt.left.label [df86c5] = 给绿船打补丁
# en: {You spend an hour with tar and a mallet. The green boat floats, briefly, with an air of surprise.|Your patch holds for a whole circuit of the boathouse. You have tar in your eyebrows and a certain pride.}
opt.left.say.1 [7acb1d] = {你拿着焦油和木槌忙了一个钟头。绿船浮了起来，短暂地，带着一脸惊讶。|你的补丁撑过了绕船屋一整圈。你眉毛上沾着焦油，心里有几分骄傲。}
# en: Carve your initials in a beam
opt.right.label [383067] = 在房梁上刻名字缩写
# en: The boatman charges a few crowns a beam.
opt.right.hint [f69342] = 船夫刻一根梁要收几枚克朗。
# en: {final_year: You pay the boatman and carve them next to a pair from sixty years ago. Somebody, one day, will run a thumb over yours and wonder.|{You pay the boatman, and your penknife snaps on the last letter. The initials stay, slightly wrong, which feels right.|You pay the boatman, find a carving that could almost be yours from long ago, and add your own beneath it.}}
opt.right.say.1 [e07860] = {final_year: 你付了船夫钱，把它刻在一对六十年前的缩写旁边。总有一天，会有人用拇指摸过你的，心生好奇。|{你付了船夫钱，最后一个字母刻到一半，小刀断了。缩写就这样留着，有点歪，感觉却刚好。|你付了船夫钱，找到一处很久以前的刻痕，几乎像是你的，于是把自己的刻在它下面。}}

@event boathouse_overheard
# en: Things Said Outside
title [bff476] = 屋外的话
# en: {Two voices out on the jetty, low and urgent. People come to the boathouse to say what they can't say indoors.|You've found the gap in the boathouse planks where every word on the jetty comes through.|Another quiet conversation on the jetty. You're starting to know the academy by its secrets.} {It sounds like a break-up.|It sounds like an apology that isn't going well.|It sounds like someone confessing to a pudding.}
text [2a1a7e] = {栈桥上有两个声音，低沉而急切。人们来船屋，是为了说屋里说不出口的话。|你发现了船屋木板上的一道缝，栈桥上的每个字都从那里漏进来。|栈桥上又一段悄悄话。你开始从秘密里认识这所学院了。} {听起来像是在分手。|听起来像是一次不太顺利的道歉。|听起来像是有人在向一块布丁告白。}
# en: Two silhouettes talking quietly on a jetty at night, seen through the slats of a boathouse wall.
scene [fbc1ce] = 夜里两个身影在栈桥上低声交谈，从船屋墙板的缝隙间望去。
# en: Listen a little longer
opt.left.label [9863e8] = 再多听一会儿
# en: {A plank creaks under you. The voices stop. Two very red faces come round the door, and now they know your face too.|An oar slides off its peg with a clatter. Footsteps; a hiss of "Who's there?"; you are, unfortunately.}
opt.left.say.1 [65cafa] = {你脚下一块木板吱嘎一响。说话声停了。两张通红的脸从门边探过来，现在他们也认得你的脸了。|一支船桨哐当一声从钉子上滑落。脚步声；一声低喝“谁在那儿？”；很不幸，是你。}
# en: {You learn more than you wanted to. You'll carry it carefully, and never tell.|It ends well, as it happens. You slip away before anyone has to know you were there.}
opt.left.say.2 [fe673b] = {你听到的比你想听的多。你会小心收好，永远不说出去。|结果是个好结局。你在有人发现之前悄悄溜走了。}
# en: Cough loudly and leave
opt.right.label [eb5a76] = 大声咳嗽，走开
# en: {They wait for you to pass, hushed and grateful. You'll never know how it ended, and that's the price.|You make a great show of looking for an oar. By the time you've found one, they've gone.}
opt.right.say.1 [4e3697] = {他们安静地等你走过，满怀感激。你永远不会知道后来怎样了，这就是代价。|你装模作样地找船桨。等你找到时，他们已经走了。}

@event orchard_under_the_trees
# en: Under the Old Trees
title [42dae6] = 老树之下
# en: {season == "spring": Blossom is coming down like snow, and {date} has some in {their} hair.|{season == "autumn": The trees are heavy with apples and wasps, and {date} is reaching for one.|{season == "winter": The orchard is bare and silver, and {date} is walking between the trees.|{date} has claimed the best of the orchard shade.}}} {{They} wave{s} you over.|{They} saw you coming before you saw {them}.|The old trees seem to expect you by now. {date} only half does.}
text [f17cc4] = {season == "spring": 花瓣像雪一样落下，{date}的头发上沾了几片。|{season == "autumn": 树上挂满了苹果和黄蜂，{date}正伸手去够一个。|{season == "winter": 果园光秃秃的，一片银白，{date}在树间散步。|{date}占了果园里最好的一片树荫。}}} {{They}招手让你过去。|你还没看见{them}，{They}就先看见了你。|老树们似乎已经习惯等你了。{date}倒没那么笃定。}
# en: Two people beneath an ancient apple tree, blossom drifting down around them like snow.
scene [f622bf] = 两个人坐在一棵古老的苹果树下，花瓣像雪一样飘落在他们周围。
# en: Stay until the light goes
opt.left.label [953fd7] = 待到天黑
# en: {season == "spring": {You stay until the blossom buries your shoes. You miss supper, and you'd do it again.|{date} picks blossom out of your hair, one petal at a time, and takes far too long about it.}|{season == "winter": {Your fingers go white, and {date} takes your hands to warm them, and doesn't give them back.|You lean against the same cold trunk until the stars come out over the bare branches.}|{You stay until the shadows outgrow the trees. You miss supper. Neither of you mentions it.|The light goes gold, then blue. {date} says something quiet you'll turn over for days.}}}
opt.left.say.1 [c3aab3] = {season == "spring": {你们一直待到花瓣埋住了鞋子。你错过了晚饭，下次还会这样。|{date}把花瓣从你头发里一片片挑出来，挑得太慢了。}|{season == "winter": {你的手指冻得发白，{date}握住你的手替你暖着，再没还给你。|你们靠着同一根冰冷的树干，直到星星爬上光秃秃的枝头。}|{你们一直待到影子比树还长。你错过了晚饭。谁也没提。|光先变成金色，又变成蓝色。{date}轻声说了句什么，你会反复回味好几天。}}}
# en: Help in the orchard together
opt.right.label [1e4a49] = 一起在果园帮忙
# en: {season == "autumn": {You fill two baskets and earn one wasp sting each. The cook gives you a pie, which you share on the steps.|{date} holds the ladder and says nothing useful, and you don't want {them} to.}|{season == "winter": {You prune dead wood side by side until your hands ache. {date} stacks it with great seriousness.|You wrap the young trees against the frost. {date} ties every knot twice.}|{season == "spring": {You carry hives along the rows for the blossom. One bee follows {date} all afternoon.|You clear the grass under the blossom. {date} keeps stopping to look up.}|{You water the young trees from a bucket chain of two. {date} is soaked by the end, and so are you.|You prop up a branch bowed with early apples. {date} holds it, and holds still, and you notice.}}}}
opt.right.say.1 [be81f6] = {season == "autumn": {你们装满了两筐，各挨了一下黄蜂蜇。厨娘给了你们一个馅饼，你们坐在台阶上分着吃了。|{date}扶着梯子，什么有用的话也没说，你也不希望{them}说。}|{season == "winter": {你们并肩修剪枯枝，直到手都酸了。{date}郑重其事地把枝条码好。|你们给小树裹上防霜的草帘。{date}每个结都系两遍。}|{season == "spring": {你们沿着树行搬蜂箱去授粉。一只蜜蜂跟了{date}一下午。|你们清理花下的杂草。{date}总是停下来抬头看。}|{你们俩排成一条水桶接力，给小树浇水。最后{date}浑身湿透，你也是。|你们撑起一根被早熟苹果压弯的枝条。{date}扶着它，一动不动，你注意到了。}}}}

@event orchard_windfalls
# en: Windfalls
title [03d58f] = 落果
# en: {The orchard trees are older than the towers, and never tidy.|The oldest tree has dropped its fruit in a ring, like a table laid for guests.|You know which tree drops what by now, and which one throws.} {season == "autumn": Pears and apples lie bruised in the grass, attended by wasps.|{season == "winter": Last year's apples lie frozen, hard as stones.|{season == "spring": It's mostly blossom, and the odd stubborn pear.|Early apples lie in the shade, small and sharp.}}}
text [7efe1c] = {果园的树比七塔还老，从来不收拾干净。|最老的那棵树把果子落成一圈，像为客人摆好的餐桌。|你现在知道哪棵树掉什么，哪棵树会砸人。} {season == "autumn": 梨和苹果磕伤了躺在草里，黄蜂在一旁看守。|{season == "winter": 去年的苹果冻在地上，硬得像石头。|{season == "spring": 大多是落花，还有几只倔强的梨。|早熟的苹果躺在树荫里，又小又酸。}}}
# en: A student gathering fallen fruit into a basket under gnarled orchard trees, older than the towers behind them.
scene [0d2ab4] = 盘曲的老果树下，一个学生把落果捡进篮子，树比身后的高塔还老。
# en: Gather windfalls to sell
opt.left.label [0a0959] = 捡落果去卖
# en: {The cook buys your basket for the cider vats and finds {season == "winter": a frozen beetle|a wasp} in it. You both pretend that's normal.|A full basket, {season == "winter": numb fingers|two stings} and a crick in your back. The crowns feel earned.}
opt.left.say.1 [cea67d] = {厨娘买下你的篮子拿去酿苹果酒，在里面发现了{season == "winter": 一只冻僵的甲虫|一只黄蜂}。你们俩都假装这很正常。|满满一篮，{season == "winter": 冻僵的手指|两处蜇伤}，外加腰酸。这些克朗挣得踏实。}
# en: Eat one under the oldest tree
opt.right.label [bfdcad] = 在最老的树下吃一个
# en: {{season == "winter": It's frozen solid. Your teeth will remember this.|There was a wasp in it. There was, briefly, a wasp in you.}|It's sour enough to turn your face inside out, and your stomach complains about it until supper. A passing first-year laughs, and so, eventually, do you.}
opt.right.say.1 [49bcf6] = {{season == "winter": 冻得像石头。你的牙会记住这一口。|里面有只黄蜂。有那么一会儿，黄蜂在你嘴里。}|酸得你五官都皱到了一起，胃一直闹到晚饭。路过的一年级生笑了，最后你也笑了。}
# en: {It's the best thing you've eaten all month. The old tree creaks, as if pleased.|You eat it slowly. Above you, the oldest tree drops one more, gently, beside your hand.}
opt.right.say.2 [d1cd02] = {这是你这个月吃过最好吃的东西。老树吱呀一声，像是很高兴。|你慢慢地吃。头顶上，最老的那棵树又轻轻落下一个，正落在你手边。}

@event orchard_cider_shed
# en: The Cider Shed
title [b0d03f] = 苹果酒棚
# en: {In the orchard shed, a few students are running an unofficial cider press.|The lookout at the cider shed has started nodding you in.|The cider shed is a fixture now. Even the lookout seems bored.} {season == "autumn": The press groans with this year's apples.|The shed smells of last autumn and wet straw.} {A goat is watching from the hedge, very carefully saying nothing.|Someone has carved a menu into the door.|A prefect's scarf hangs on a nail, unexplained.}
text [8c11d7] = {果园的棚子里，几个学生在偷偷经营一台苹果酒榨机。|苹果酒棚望风的人开始点头放你进去了。|苹果酒棚已经成了固定去处。连望风的都显得无聊了。} {season == "autumn": 榨机被今年的苹果压得吱嘎作响。|棚里一股去年秋天和湿稻草的味道。} {一只山羊在树篱边看着，非常小心地一言不发。|有人在门上刻了一份酒单。|钉子上挂着一条级长的围巾，来历不明。}
# en: A tumbledown orchard shed with a wooden cider press inside, three students turning the screw and a fourth keeping watch at the door.
scene [31b8c3] = 破旧的果园棚子里有一台木制苹果酒榨机，三个学生在拧螺杆，第四个在门口望风。
# en: Buy a cup
opt.left.label [e3b76c] = 买一杯
# en: {A prefect turns up as you raise the cup. Everyone is suddenly very interested in apples.|The lookout whistles too late. A prefect takes your name, then, after some thought, your cup.}
opt.left.say.1 [af521a] = {你刚举起杯子，一个级长就出现了。大家突然都对苹果产生了浓厚兴趣。|望风的口哨吹晚了。一个级长记下你的名字，想了想，又没收了你的杯子。}
# en: {It's sharp, cold and a little bit fizzy. The day goes golden at the edges.|You drink it on an upturned bucket while someone tells a story about a goose. Excellent cider. Better goose.}
opt.left.say.2 [6f62de] = {酒又酸又凉，还有一点点气泡。这一天的边缘都变成了金色。|你坐在倒扣的桶上喝，有人在讲一只鹅的故事。酒很好。鹅更好。}
# en: Help turn the press, for a share
opt.right.label [297dd0] = 帮忙榨酒，换一份
# en: {You turn the screw until your shoulders burn. The second-year in charge teaches you why some apples are better bruised.|You're sticky to the elbows and you've learned more about fermentation than in a term of class.}
opt.right.say.1 [0f12cb] = {你拧螺杆拧到肩膀火辣辣地疼。主事的二年级生教你为什么有些苹果磕伤了反而更好。|你黏到了胳膊肘，学到的发酵知识比一学期的课还多。}

@event maud_cottage_kettle
# en: Tea at Maud's
title [14a007] = 莫德家的茶
# en: {Old Maud's kettle is nearly boiling, as it always is. "Sit down, dearie," she says. "You look like a puddle with a worry."|The kettle is nearly boiling. Maud has already put out your cup, the chipped one.|Your chipped cup is waiting. Maud says it's been asking after you.} {Bartholomew is eating a tea towel.|Rain drums on the thatch.|A hen is asleep on the windowsill.|Bees drone in the eaves.}
text [00c2be] = {老莫德的水壶快要开了，一向如此。“坐吧，亲爱的，”她说，“你看着像个犯愁的水洼。”|水壶快要开了。莫德已经摆好了你的杯子，那只有缺口的。|你那只有缺口的杯子在等你。莫德说它一直在打听你。} {巴塞洛缪在吃一条茶巾。|雨点敲着茅草屋顶。|一只母鸡睡在窗台上。|蜜蜂在屋檐下嗡嗡作响。}
# en: A low cottage kitchen, a kettle on the hob, an old woman pouring tea into a chipped cup, a goat's head poking through the open door.
scene [20892a] = 低矮的小屋厨房，炉上坐着水壶，一位老妇人往有缺口的杯子里倒茶，一只山羊从敞开的门外探进头来。
# en: Stay for a second cup
opt.left.label [0720c4] = 再喝一杯
# en: {Maud tells you a sad story the way other people give a recipe. You walk home late and cold, thinking about it.|"Never trust a dry spring, dearie," she says. You won't understand it for a fortnight.|The second cup becomes a third. It's dark when you leave, and you've only half noticed.}
opt.left.say.1 [88985a] = {莫德像别人讲菜谱那样讲了一个伤心的故事。你很晚才冒着寒气走回去，一路想着它。|“永远别信干燥的春天，亲爱的，”她说。两个星期后你才会明白。|第二杯变成了第三杯。你离开时天已经黑了，你几乎没察觉。}
# en: Ask her for a remedy
opt.right.label [72f493] = 向她讨个偏方
# en: {She brews you something that tastes of ditches. "Down in one, dearie." You feel better at once, and resent it.|"For what ails you," she says, and doesn't say what she thinks that is. It tastes of nettles and of being right.}
opt.right.say.1 [a08f35] = {她给你熬了一碗沟渠味的东西。“一口喝干，亲爱的。”你立刻好多了，并为此愤愤不平。|“治你的毛病，”她说，却没说她觉得你是什么毛病。那味道像荨麻，也像她说对了。}

@event maud_cottage_bartholomew
# en: Bartholomew Is Out
title [e4bd17] = 巴塞洛缪跑了
# en: {Bartholomew the goat has got out.|Bartholomew is out again, and has learned to lift the gate latch with his teeth.|Bartholomew has escaped so often that the hens no longer scatter.} {slot == "evening": Maud doesn't even look up from her knitting.|Maud's note on the door says she's at the greenhouses, and to mind the goat.} {He has eaten half a washing line.|He is standing on the roof of the henhouse, looking pleased.|He is in the cabbages, conducting a slow and thorough war.}
text [b77b4f] = {巴塞洛缪跑出来了。|巴塞洛缪又跑出来了，它学会了用牙齿抬门闩。|巴塞洛缪跑得太勤，母鸡们都懒得四散奔逃了。} {slot == "evening": 莫德连头都不从针线活上抬。|门上莫德留的字条说她去温室了，让人看好山羊。} {它已经吃掉了半根晾衣绳。|它站在鸡舍顶上，一脸得意。|它在卷心菜地里，打一场缓慢而彻底的战争。}
# en: A goat standing triumphantly on the roof of a henhouse, chickens scattering, a student approaching with an apple held out.
scene [d9f8cd] = 一只山羊得意洋洋地站在鸡舍顶上，鸡群四散，一个学生举着苹果靠近。
# en: Chase him down
opt.left.label [f61b49] = 把它追回来
# en: {You corner him by the water butt. He gives up with the air of someone who allowed it. {slot == "evening": "Ta, dearie," calls Maud.|You tie him to the gate and leave Maud a note.}|You catch him on the second lap. He chews your sleeve all the way back, as a souvenir.}
opt.left.say.1 [510f86] = {你在接雨水的桶边把它堵住了。它投降的样子像是在施舍你。{slot == "evening": “谢啦，亲爱的，”莫德喊道。|你把它拴在门上，给莫德留了张字条。}|你在第二圈抓住了它。它一路嚼着你的袖子回去，当作纪念品。}
# en: {He leads you twice round the orchard and once through the hen run, then trots home on his own.|You end up in the cabbages. Bartholomew watches you from the roof, chewing, unhurried.}
opt.left.say.2 [e2fbb8] = {它领着你绕果园跑了两圈，又穿过鸡圈一回，然后自己溜达回家了。|你最后栽进了卷心菜地。巴塞洛缪站在屋顶上看着你，嚼着东西，不慌不忙。}
# en: Bribe him with your lunch
opt.right.label [eb4050] = 拿午饭贿赂它
# en: {He takes your sandwich and follows you home like a gentleman. You go hungry until supper.|Your lunch disappears in three bites. Bartholomew looks at you as if you might be worth knowing.}
opt.right.say.1 [dfc2b5] = {它接过你的三明治，像位绅士一样跟你回家。你一直饿到晚饭。|你的午饭三口就没了。巴塞洛缪看着你，像是觉得你或许值得结交。}

@event maud_cottage_top_shelf
# en: The Top Shelf
title [fd2f93] = 最高一层架子
# en: {{slot == "evening": Maud has stepped out to the hens.|Maud is up at the greenhouses.} The top shelf of jars is right there, every label in her spidery hand.|Maud has stepped out, and the top shelf has gained a jar since you were last here.|You know the top shelf by heart, except for whichever jar Maud added last.} One label reads {"not for you, dearie"|"only in emergencies"|"do not shake"}, and the jar is {glowing faintly|humming|warm to the touch}.
text [523727] = {{slot == "evening": 莫德出去喂鸡了。|莫德去温室了。}最高一层的罐子就在眼前，每张标签都是她那蜘蛛似的笔迹。|莫德出去了，最高一层比你上次来时多了个罐子。|最高一层你已经烂熟于心，只有莫德最近添的那个罐子除外。}其中一张标签写着{“不是给你的，亲爱的”|“仅限紧急情况”|“切勿摇晃”}，那罐子{发着微光|在嗡嗡作响|摸上去是温的}。
# en: A high cottage shelf crowded with stoppered jars and handwritten labels, one jar glowing faintly blue.
scene [c62b98] = 小屋里高高的架子上挤满了塞着瓶塞的罐子和手写标签，其中一罐发着淡淡的蓝光。
# en: Open it, just a little
opt.left.label [73d5dd] = 打开一点点
# en: {Something sweet and blue drifts out and settles in your chest. You feel, briefly, enormous.|A breath of summer rain escapes. You put the lid back on smiling.}
opt.left.say.1 [42b612] = {一缕甜甜的蓝色飘出来，落进你的胸口。有那么一会儿，你觉得自己无比庞大。|一口夏雨的气息逃了出来。你笑着把盖子盖了回去。}
# en: {Your eyebrows turn the colour of the label. When Maud sees them, she says nothing whatsoever.|It sneezes. Then you sneeze, for an hour. "Told you, dearie," says Maud later, not unkindly.}
opt.left.say.2 [a35ec8] = {你的眉毛变成了标签的颜色。莫德看见后，一个字也没说。|它打了个喷嚏。然后你打了一个钟头的喷嚏。“早说过了，亲爱的，”莫德后来说，语气并不凶。}
# en: Dust the shelf instead
opt.right.label [cb81d8] = 改为掸掸灰
# en: {You dust every jar and read every label. Maud's handwriting is a whole education, if a strange one.|Maud finds a clean shelf. "Somebody's been learning," she says, which isn't quite thanks.}
opt.right.say.1 [80537a] = {你掸了每个罐子，读了每张标签。莫德的笔迹本身就是一门学问，虽然古怪。|莫德发现架子干干净净。“有人在长学问了，”她说，这不太算道谢。}

@event secret_garden_humming_pear
# en: The Humming Pear
title [041751] = 哼歌的梨树
# en: {The pear tree in Maud's secret garden is humming to itself.|The pear tree has changed its tune since you were last here, as if it's been practising.|The pear tree hums when you come in now. You'd like to think it's for you.} {season == "winter": Its tune is low and slow, like something asleep.|{season == "spring": Its tune has gone quick and bright with blossom.|{Its tune is one you almost know.|Its tune has a sad turn in the middle.}}}
text [3861ee] = {莫德秘密花园里的梨树在自顾自地哼歌。|自你上次来过，梨树换了个调子，像是一直在练习。|现在你一进来，梨树就开始哼歌。你愿意相信那是为你哼的。} {season == "winter": 它的调子又低又慢，像某种在沉睡的东西。|{season == "spring": 它的调子随着开花变得轻快明亮。|{那是一支你几乎会唱的曲子。|那支曲子中间有个忧伤的转折。}}}
# en: A student lying in the grass under a pear tree in a hidden walled garden, ferns glowing softly around them.
scene [69e58c] = 隐蔽的围墙花园里，一个学生躺在梨树下的草地上，周围的蕨类柔柔发光。
# en: Hum along with it
opt.left.label [d18c15] = 跟着它一起哼
# en: {You find the harmony on the third try. The tree corrects you twice, kindly.|The two of you hum until the ferns glow brighter. Afterwards you can't get the tune out of your head for days.}
opt.left.say.1 [5dfbb8] = {第三次你才找到和声。梨树温和地纠正了你两次。|你们一起哼，直到蕨类更亮了。之后好几天，那调子都在你脑子里挥之不去。}
# en: Nap in its shade
opt.right.label [981938] = 在树荫下打个盹
# en: {You wake rested, a few crowns lighter, with a fresh root curled over the spot where they fell.|You sleep like a seed. A few crowns slip out of your pocket and the roots close over them. Rent, perhaps.}
opt.right.say.1 [3b207d] = {你醒来时神清气爽，口袋里少了几枚克朗，掉落的地方盘着一条新长的根。|你睡得像一颗种子。几枚克朗从口袋滑出，树根把它们合拢了。大概是房租吧。}
# en: You sleep like a seed and wake with your empty pocket turned out, as if the roots had checked.
opt.right.say.2 [85a98a] = 你睡得像一颗种子，醒来时空口袋被翻了出来，仿佛树根检查过了。

@event secret_garden_silver_bees
# en: The Silver Bees
title [1eab66] = 银蜂
# en: {The silver bees are working the ferns; their hive in the old stump drips honey the colour of moonlight.|The silver bees have built a second comb, lopsided, as if in a hurry.|The silver bees know you now, more or less.} {season == "winter": Even in winter they fly, slowly, like snow going the wrong way.|{The comb is fuller than you've ever seen it.|One of them lands on your sleeve and stays.|They're dancing a direction you can't read.}}
text [2aba13] = {银蜂在蕨类间忙碌；老树桩里的蜂巢淌着月光色的蜂蜜。|银蜂又筑了第二块蜂巢，歪歪扭扭，像是赶工。|银蜂现在或多或少认得你了。} {season == "winter": 即使在冬天它们也在飞，慢慢的，像飘错了方向的雪。|{蜂巢比你见过的任何时候都满。|一只落在你的袖子上，不走了。|它们跳着一个你读不懂的方向。}}
# en: Bees made of silver light hovering around a hive in a hollow stump, a student reaching carefully towards a dripping comb.
scene [db712c] = 银光构成的蜜蜂绕着空心树桩里的蜂巢盘旋，一个学生小心翼翼地伸手去取滴蜜的蜂巢。
# en: Take a little comb
opt.left.label [9d8f0c] = 取一小块蜂巢
# en: {A silver sting feels like a cold spark. Your hand glows for an hour and aches for two.|The bees file a complaint, in the form of your thumb.}
opt.left.say.1 [6eaf76] = {被银蜂蜇一下，像一颗冰冷的火星。你的手亮了一个钟头，又疼了两个钟头。|蜜蜂提出了抗议——抗议书就是你肿起来的拇指。}
# en: {You take a thumb's width of comb. It tastes like starlight and burns a little going down.|The bees let you take a little, and watch to make sure it's only a little.}
opt.left.say.2 [8623e2] = {你取了拇指宽的一小块。尝起来像星光，咽下去有点烫。|蜜蜂让你取了一点，还盯着确保真的只有一点。}
# en: Follow a bee home
opt.right.label [3d2092] = 跟着一只蜜蜂回家
# en: {The bee leads you through brambles to a fern you've never seen, and then leaves you there, scratched and curious.|You follow it all the way round the garden and back to the stump. It seems to find this funny.}
opt.right.say.1 [694dfc] = {蜜蜂领你穿过荆棘，来到一株你从没见过的蕨类前，然后把你丢在那儿，满身划痕，满心好奇。|你跟着它绕花园一圈，又回到树桩。它似乎觉得这很好笑。}

@event secret_garden_glowing_ferns
# en: The Glowing Ferns
title [725061] = 发光的蕨类
# en: {The ferns in the secret garden glow when the light goes. One frond would light your dormitory for a week. Maud said not to pick them.|Since your last visit a new fern has unfurled by the gate, already glowing.|The ferns glow. You know exactly what a frond is worth, and what Maud said.} {One has grown over the path, right at your hand.|A broken frond lies on the ground already, still glowing.|They're brighter than you've ever seen them.}
text [f2564e] = {天色一暗，秘密花园里的蕨类就亮了。一片叶子就能把你的宿舍照亮一个星期。莫德说过不许摘。|自你上次来过，门边又舒展开一株新蕨，已经亮了。|蕨类在发光。你清楚一片叶子值多少，也清楚莫德说过什么。} {有一株长到了小路上，正在你手边。|地上已经有一片折断的叶子，还在发光。|它们比你见过的任何时候都亮。}
# en: A hidden garden at dusk, waist-high ferns glowing pale green, one student crouched with fingers near a frond.
scene [cac6b0] = 黄昏时的隐秘花园，齐腰高的蕨类发着淡绿色的光，一个学生蹲着，手指靠近一片叶子。
# en: Pick a single frond
opt.left.label [ed6b96] = 只摘一片
# en: {The frond goes dark before you reach the door. The garden feels a little colder to you the next time.|The frond curls up in your hand like a woodlouse and goes out. The silver bees follow you to the gate, accusingly.}
opt.left.say.1 [4d9cc6] = {还没走到门口，那片叶子就暗了。下次来时，花园对你冷淡了一些。|叶子在你手里像鼠妇一样蜷起来，熄灭了。银蜂一路跟你到门口，满是责备。}
# en: {It lights your dormitory green for a week. You read by it, and feel very slightly watched.|You keep it in a jar by your bed. It glows softer every night, like something being polite.}
opt.left.say.2 [357809] = {它把你的宿舍照成绿色，亮了一个星期。你借着它读书，总觉得有一点点被注视。|你把它放在床边的罐子里。它一夜比一夜暗，像在客气。}
# en: Leave them glowing
opt.right.label [76d055] = 让它们继续发光
# en: {You sit and watch the glow instead, and learn the way it moves with your breath. Maud would approve, if she knew.|You leave them be. On the way out, the ferns lean after you, like a dog that wanted to come.}
opt.right.say.1 [f02473] = {你坐下来看那光，发现它随着你的呼吸起伏。莫德要是知道，会赞许的。|你没去碰它们。离开时，蕨类朝你的方向倾着，像一只想跟来的狗。}

@event courier_loft_letter_home
# en: A Letter Home
title [8bce33] = 一封家书
# en: {The courier loft will take a letter home for next to nothing. You've meant to write for weeks.|This time the letter has been half-written in your head since breakfast.|Writing home is a habit now, and the loft knows your handwriting.} {final_year: There aren't many letters left to send from here.|{season == "winter": Frost on the window; the pigeonholes stuffed with cards.|{The dispatch bell rings twice while you write.|A broken broom leans against your elbow.}}}
text [2f3311] = {信使阁楼花不了几个钱就能帮你把信送回家。你已经想写好几个星期了。|这一封从早饭起就在你脑子里写了一半。|往家里写信成了习惯，阁楼也认得你的笔迹了。} {final_year: 能从这里寄出的信不多了。|{season == "winter": 窗上结着霜，信格里塞满了贺卡。|{你写信时，发件铃响了两次。|一把坏扫帚靠在你胳膊肘边。}}}
# en: A draughty loft full of pigeonholes, a student writing a letter on a parcel by the light of a high window.
scene [953afc] = 满是信格的透风阁楼里，一个学生借着高窗的光，在一个包裹上写信。
# en: Write it all down and send it
opt.left.label [2de5e0] = 全写下来寄出去
# en: {You write three pages and post them before you can cross anything out. You feel lighter, and a little homesick.|You tell them about your classes, and not about the hard parts. Then, in a postscript, you tell them about the hard parts.}
opt.left.say.1 [302029] = {你写了三页，在来得及划掉任何一句之前就寄了出去。你觉得轻松了些，也有点想家。|你跟他们讲了你的课，没讲难处。然后，在附言里，你讲了难处。}
# en: Write it, then don't send it
opt.right.label [cf5f6f] = 写好了，但不寄
# en: {You read it over and fold it into your pocket instead. Some letters are only for writing.|You keep this one. The courier asks if you're sure. You aren't.}
opt.right.say.1 [e13306] = {你读了一遍，折好放进口袋。有些信只是用来写的。|这封你留下了。信使问你确定吗。你并不确定。}

@event courier_loft_dispatch_bell
# en: The Dispatch Bell
title [e813ff] = 发件铃
# en: {The dispatch bell clangs and the loft explodes into brooms. A courier shoves a parcel at you. "You've got legs. Lecture tower!"|The couriers have started eyeing the ladder whenever someone climbs it.|The bell. A parcel. A look. You know the drill.} {The parcel is ticking.|The parcel is addressed to "Whoever Is On Duty".|The parcel is very cold.}
text [fcbf9d] = {发件铃一响，阁楼里扫帚乱飞。一个信使把包裹塞给你。“你有腿。讲堂塔！”|现在每次有人爬梯子，信使们都会瞟上一眼。|铃声。包裹。一个眼神。你知道该怎么做。} {包裹在滴答作响。|包裹上写着“寄给值班的随便谁”。|包裹冰凉冰凉的。}
# en: A chaotic loft as a dispatch bell clangs, couriers grabbing brooms and parcels, one holding a parcel out to a visitor.
scene [b87d28] = 发件铃大作，乱成一团的阁楼里信使们抓起扫帚和包裹，其中一个把包裹递给来客。
# en: Run the parcel across campus
opt.left.label [71bfc4] = 跑一趟送包裹
# en: {You get it there out of breath and in time. The tip is a few crowns and a very strange look.|You run it up four flights of stairs. The recipient signs for it without looking up, as if you were the post.}
opt.left.say.1 [72a549] = {你气喘吁吁但准时送到了。小费是几枚克朗外加一个非常奇怪的眼神。|你跑上四层楼。收件人头也不抬就签了字，好像你本来就是邮差。}
# en: Hand it back, politely
opt.right.label [b4d5ae] = 客气地还回去
# en: {"Fine, fine," says the courier, already on a broom. You hear about it, loudly, from the rafters.|The courier takes it back with a sigh that follows you down the ladder.}
opt.right.say.1 [af15f9] = {“行吧行吧，”信使说着已经跨上了扫帚。你从椽子上方听到了响亮的抱怨。|信使叹着气接回包裹，那声叹息一路跟着你下了梯子。}

@event courier_loft_broom_rack
# en: The Fast Broom
title [0775c7] = 快扫帚
# en: {At the end of the rack is the courier loft's fast broom, tagged in red. Couriers only. Nobody's watching.|The fast broom is back on the rack, red tag and all.|The red-tagged broom. You've thought about it every time you've come up here.} {season == "winter": The loft doors are open on a sky full of snow.|{The loft doors stand open on a blue sky.|Someone has polished it recently.|The red tag has a fresh scorch mark.}}
text [e04714] = {架子尽头是信使阁楼的快扫帚，挂着红牌。仅限信使。没人在看。|快扫帚又回到了架子上，红牌也在。|那把挂红牌的扫帚。每次上来你都会想到它。} {season == "winter": 阁楼的门敞着，外面是漫天飞雪。|{阁楼的门敞着，外面是蓝天。|最近有人给它上过油。|红牌上有一道新焦痕。}}
# en: A rack of courier brooms in a loft, one sleek black broom set apart from the others with a red tag on its handle.
scene [76169f] = 阁楼里一排信使扫帚，其中一把光滑的黑扫帚单独放着，柄上挂着红牌。
# en: Take it for one lap
opt.left.label [c03fc1] = 骑它飞一圈
# en: {One lap of the towers, fast enough to make your ears sing. You put it back with the bristles barely warm.|You fly it under the bridges of light and come back laughing. Nobody saw, except, possibly, everybody.}
opt.left.say.1 [f78b92] = {绕七塔一圈，快得耳朵嗡嗡响。你放回去时，帚毛几乎没热。|你骑着它从光之桥底下穿过，笑着飞回来。没人看见，除了，也许，所有人。}
# en: {It knows you aren't a courier. It shows you the courtyard, very close up.|It bucks you off into a haystack outside the stables. The stable hand laughs about it for a week.}
opt.left.say.2 [4fc2f8] = {它知道你不是信使。它让你近距离地看了看庭院的地面。|它把你甩进了马厩外的干草堆。马夫为这事笑了一个星期。}
# en: Tighten its bristles instead
opt.right.label [8b8ed8] = 改为给它紧紧帚毛
# en: {You spend an hour learning how a good broom is bound. It's more satisfying than you'd admit.|You retie the bristles properly. Some courier will fly a little faster tomorrow and never know why.}
opt.right.say.1 [84789c] = {你花了一个钟头学一把好扫帚是怎么扎成的。这比你愿意承认的更让人满足。|你把帚毛重新扎好。明天会有个信使飞得快一点，却永远不知道为什么。}

@event whisperwood_sleeptalk
# en: The Forest Talks
title [380652] = 森林在说话
# en: {The Whisperwood is talking in its sleep. You stand very still to make out the words.|You've started to catch whole words in the forest's mumbling.|You've learned to stand still and let the forest talk.} Today it's {listing trees that were felled|arguing about the rain|saying a name, over and over, that isn't yours}. {season == "winter": Snow muffles half of it.|{season == "autumn": Leaves fall with every word.|Fog moves between the trunks.}}
text [27381d] = {低语森林在说梦话。你一动不动地站着，想听清那些词。|你开始能听清森林嘟囔里的整个词了。|你已经学会静静站着，让森林说下去。}今天它在{列举被砍倒的树|为下雨的事争吵|一遍遍念着一个不是你的名字}。{season == "winter": 雪捂住了一半。|{season == "autumn": 每说一个字就落下一片叶子。|雾在树干间游移。}}
# en: A student standing very still in a misty old forest, head tilted, as if listening to the trees.
scene [9d0c9e] = 雾气弥漫的古老森林里，一个学生一动不动地站着，侧着头，像是在听树说话。
# en: Listen closely
opt.left.label [21f0ed] = 仔细听
# en: {You catch a whole sentence. It's about a winter long ago, and it's sad, and you walk home with it.|It notices you listening and goes quiet, the way a sleeper does. You leave feeling rude.}
opt.left.say.1 [5a9c31] = {你听清了完整的一句。那是关于很久以前的一个冬天，很悲伤，你带着它走回了家。|它发现你在听，便像睡着的人那样安静下来。你离开时觉得自己很失礼。}
# en: Walk on, humming
opt.right.label [f1a5bc] = 哼着歌继续走
# en: {You walk the long loop humming loudly. The forest grumbles and turns over. You come back with muddy boots and a clear head.|You hum all the way round. Twice, the forest hums back.}
opt.right.say.1 [e2e20f] = {你大声哼着歌走完长长的一圈。森林嘟囔着翻了个身。你带着一靴子泥和清醒的脑袋回来。|你一路哼着歌。有两次，森林也哼了回来。}

@event whisperwood_foragers
# en: Foraging Season
title [067bb9] = 采集季
# en: {season == "autumn": The Whisperwood is full of mushrooms and students with baskets.|{season == "winter": A few hardy foragers are scraping lichen off the oaks.|{season == "spring": The clearings are thick with wild garlic and foragers.|The brambles are heavy with berries, and so are the foragers.}}} {A second-year from Rootward waves you over.|The Rootward forager is back, and saves you a spot.|The foragers treat you as one of their own now.}
text [62e283] = {season == "autumn": 低语森林里满是蘑菇和提着篮子的学生。|{season == "winter": 几个不怕冷的采集者在刮橡树上的地衣。|{season == "spring": 林间空地长满了野蒜，也挤满了采集者。|荆棘丛上挂满了浆果，采集者身上也挂满了。}}} {一个根庐的二年级生朝你招手。|那个根庐的采集者又来了，给你留了个位置。|采集者们现在把你当自己人了。}
# en: A handful of students with baskets crouching in a forest clearing, one holding up a mushroom for the others to inspect.
scene [6bbb73] = 几个提篮子的学生蹲在林间空地上，其中一个举起一只蘑菇给其他人看。
# en: Forage for the apothecary
opt.left.label [c317dd] = 为药铺采集
# en: {Pell & Daughters buys your basket and throws out a third of it. You've still got nettle rash.|A good basket, a fair price, and brambles in places you'd rather not discuss.}
opt.left.say.1 [c63071] = {佩尔父女药铺收下你的篮子，扔掉了三分之一。你身上的荨麻疹还在。|一篮好货，一个公道价，还有一些你不愿细说的地方扎进了荆棘。}
# en: Learn the plants from the expert
opt.right.label [5629c5] = 跟行家认植物
# en: {The second-year names everything, twice, with its uses and its poisons. You come away full of names and short of patience.|You learn which mushroom is supper and which is a funeral. It takes until supper, and you'll need it.}
opt.right.say.1 [1def08] = {那个二年级生把每样东西都说了两遍，连用途带毒性。你满脑子名字，耐心所剩无几。|你学会了分辨哪种蘑菇是晚餐，哪种是葬礼。一直学到晚饭时分，你会用得上的。}

@event whisperwood_off_path
# en: The Path That Wasn't
title [916a4a] = 本不存在的小路
# en: {A path opens to your left that wasn't there last time.|Another path that wasn't there before. The Whisperwood does this.|The wood has offered you a new path again. You're starting to think it likes you.} {It's lined with pale stones.|It smells of woodsmoke where there's no fire.|It goes downhill, which is wrong, because you're at the bottom of the hill.}
text [3b11a8] = {你左手边出现了一条上次没有的小路。|又一条以前没有的小路。低语森林就是这样。|森林又给你开了一条新路。你开始觉得它喜欢你。} {路边排着苍白的石头。|没有火，却闻得到柴烟味。|它往下坡走，这不对，因为你已经在山脚了。}
# en: A narrow path branching off into fog between old trees, a student pausing at the fork with a hand on a marked trunk.
scene [a1f31c] = 古树间一条窄路分岔伸进雾里，一个学生在岔口停下，手扶着一棵做了记号的树干。
# en: Follow it a little way
opt.left.label [03da75] = 跟着走一小段
# en: {It leads to a clearing you'll never find again, full of moonpetal buds. You come back with a pocketful of quiet.|It loops you round to an old stone with words on it. You copy them down. They mean nothing yet.}
opt.left.say.1 [e431d9] = {它通向一片你再也找不到的空地，开满了月瓣花的花苞。你带回了满满一口袋的安静。|它绕着你来到一块刻着字的老石头前。你把字抄了下来。它们暂时还没有意义。}
# en: {You walk in circles until dusk and come out at the lake, with no idea how.|The path ends at a wall of fog. Turning back takes much longer than going in did.}
opt.left.say.2 [309920] = {你转圈转到黄昏，出来时到了湖边，不知道是怎么走到的。|小路尽头是一堵雾墙。往回走比进来花的时间长得多。}
# en: Mark a tree and turn back
opt.right.label [851506] = 在树上做记号，回头
# en: {You carve an arrow in the bark. The next time you come, the arrow points somewhere else.|You turn back. The path watches you go, and quietly closes behind you.}
opt.right.say.1 [b23549] = {你在树皮上刻了个箭头。下次来时，箭头指向了别处。|你转身回去。小路目送你离开，在你身后悄悄合上了。}
